// ============================================================================
// detection/0A — Malicious-tenant tripwire rule (Continuous/NRT-eligible)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// STATUS  : Written and staged — NOT DEPLOYED. See detection/README.md.
// Surface : Defender XDR Advanced Hunting — Custom Detection Rule query
// Cadence : Continuous (NRT). NRT rules accept SINGLE-TABLE queries only —
//           no join / union / summarize; where/extend/project-family
//           operators. This file obeys that: EmailUrlInfo alone, row-shaped
//           operators only. It also runs unchanged manually or on a timed
//           cadence.
// Table   : EmailUrlInfo (only)
// Role    : The alarm the whole detection track exists to feed: ANY mail URL
//           pointing at a maliciousTenants entry alerts as the record
//           arrives — delivery time, before anyone clicks. Fast and cheap
//           because trust was decided ahead of time by the list program
//           (1 → 2 → 3 → 00-shared-lists → here).
// Traded for NRT (and where each piece lives instead):
//           - unknown-tenant click/burst gates → detection/0b (hourly
//             behavioural rule), incident/1a/1b (manual triage) and
//             detection/1 (weekly review queue) — NRT cannot join
//             EmailEvents/UrlClickEvents
//           - Recipient/Subject columns → not in EmailUrlInfo, so this rule
//             ALERTS but takes no email actions; containment is incident/2
//             with the tenant key, which is the standing workflow anyway.
// Caveats : 1. If rule creation rejects the query for lacking an
//              impacted-asset column (EmailUrlInfo has none of the
//              account/device/recipient columns), use the UrlClickEvents
//              variant in detection/README.md — same tripwire, has
//              AccountUpn, but fires on click instead of delivery.
//           2. If the editor rejects the `let` statement, inline the list:
//              | where SpTenant in ("badtenant1", "badtenant2")
// MIRROR  : maliciousTenants must stay in sync with 00-shared-lists.kql and
//           its other consumers (detection/0b, incident/1a, incident/1b,
//           detection/1, detection/3).
// ============================================================================
let lookback = 1h;   // manual-run window; effectively ignored under NRT streaming
let maliciousTenants = dynamic([
    // sync from 00-shared-lists.kql — empty list = rule produces nothing
]);
EmailUrlInfo
| where Timestamp > ago(lookback)
| where UrlDomain endswith ".sharepoint.com"
| extend SpTenant = extract(@"^([a-z0-9-]+?)(?:-my)?\.sharepoint\.com$", 1, tolower(UrlDomain))
| where isnotempty(SpTenant)
| where SpTenant in (maliciousTenants)
| extend Classification = "Malicious",
         Severity       = "P1-High"
| project
    Timestamp,
    ReportId,
    NetworkMessageId,
    Url,
    UrlDomain,
    UrlLocation,
    SpTenant,
    Classification,
    Severity
